    "voice": {
      "learned": true,
      "tone": "Warm, playful, lightly whimsical copy that treats everyday paper goods as small occasions for delight; declarative and a little aspirational without being salesy or hyperbolic.",
      "rhythm": "Short, often fragmentary sentences stacked two or three to a paragraph ('Every cover, a work of art. Consider your desk the gallery.'); occasional longer sentence built on a comma or em-dash to add a second, softer beat after a plain statement.",
      "person": "Writes as 'we' / the brand collectively; addresses the reader as 'you' and 'your'. No individual signer in body copy; named humans (e.g. a Design Director) appear only inside quoted asides, not as the narrating voice.",
      "greetings": [],
      "sign_offs": [],
      "exemplars": [
        "Every season, a new collection takes shape – designed by hand in our London studio. Every cover, a work of art. Consider your desk the gallery.",
        "Founded in 2015, Papier invites magic into the everyday with premium paper treasures for every desk. Whether setting out your wildest dreams on a page or scribbling a to-do list to get you ready for the day – stationery is a space to think, to connect, to plan, to celebrate.",
        "We believe that *STATIONERY* is more than pen and paper. It’s a powerful way to make each day *NOTEWORTHY*.",
        "Make your pages feel like you. Put a name, favourite quote or meaningful motto on the cover of your Papier pieces for free.",
        "Our days have never asked more of our attention. Between lectures, deadlines, notifications and shared calendars, planning has become another thing we do on our screens. Yet every semester, students and teachers continue to reach for paper."
      ],
